data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":1006,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_04de6b92baab60ea016adb45a9b39c81919200003b6bbd3433","call_id":"call_e6dd3bf20c9b469c97613eba9baa7284","name":"check_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_candidate\":24,\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/1/locals\",\"value\":[{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"positive real\",\"scope\":\"R002\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary t>0.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"J\",\"type\":\"compact interval in (0,∞) containing t in its interior\",\"scope\":\"R002\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Set J=[t/2,3t/2].\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"t\"]},{\"symbol\":\"C\",\"type\":\"compact subset of ℝⁿ\",\"scope\":\"R002\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose compact C from H003 for J.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"H003\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"J\"]},{\"symbol\":\"K\",\"type\":\"compact subset of ℝⁿ\",\"scope\":\"R002\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix an arbitrary compact K⊂ℝⁿ to establish finiteness on every compact.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\"]},{\"symbol\":\"R₀\",\"type\":\"positive real\",\"scope\":\"R002\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose R₀>0 with K⊂closedBall(0,R₀) from F001.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"K\"]},{\"symbol\":\"Q\",\"type\":\"closed coordinate box [-R₀,R₀]^n\",\"scope\":\"R002\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Set Q=∏_{i=1}^n[-R₀,R₀].\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"R₀\",\"n\"]}]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/1/argument\",\"value\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"Fix arbitrary t>0, set J=[t/2,3t/2], and choose compact C from H003 so u(x,s)=q for every x∉C and s∈J. To prove Lebesgue measure finite on every compact, fix arbitrary compact K⊂ℝⁿ. By M016, K is bounded. In the Euclidean norm, boundedness implies there is R₀>0 such that every x∈K satisfies ‖x‖≤R₀; record this as F001: ∃R₀>0, ∀x∈K, ‖x‖≤R₀. The local witness will be chosen from this proved existence in the next paragraph.\",\"uses\":[\"H003\",\"M016\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"t\",\"J\",\"C\",\"K\",\"n\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"There exists R₀>0 such that every x∈K satisfies ‖x‖≤R₀.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"K\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Choose R₀ using F001 and define Q=∏_{i=1}^n[-R₀,R₀]. Each coordinate has absolute value at most ‖x‖, hence K⊆Q. M013 and M014 give μ(Q)=∏_{i=1}^n μ([-R₀,R₀])=(2R₀)^n<∞. Since K is compact in the Hausdorff Euclidean space, it is closed and therefore Borel measurable; monotonicity yields μ(K)≤μ(Q)<∞. As K was arbitrary, Lebesgue measure is finite on compact sets. The Borel measurable structure on ℝⁿ is the σ-algebra generated by the Euclidean open sets, so opens are measurable. Joint smoothness and u=q on the open spatial complement of C throughout J imply all first spatial and time derivatives, and the second and mixed derivatives entering e_t, vanish outside C. Thus e(·,t) is continuous with compact support in C. Apply M001 to conclude e(·,t) is integrable. The same smoothness/support argument shows u_t(·,s), u_{x_j}(·,s), e(·,s), and e_t(·,s) are continuous and vanish off C for each s∈J and j=1,…,n. This proves N001 for arbitrary t>0.\",\"uses\":[\"M013\",\"M014\",\"M001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"R₀\",\"Q\",\"K\",\"C\",\"J\",\"e\",\"u\",\"n\",\"m\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}]}]} }","status":"completed"}}

