aration\":\"Choose compact C from H003 for J.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"H003\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"J\"]},{\"symbol\":\"K\",\"type\":\"compact subset of ℝⁿ\",\"scope\":\"R002\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix an arbitrary compact K⊂ℝⁿ to establish finiteness on every compact.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\"]},{\"symbol\":\"R₀\",\"type\":\"positive real\",\"scope\":\"R002\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose R₀>0 with K⊂closedBall(0,R₀) from F001.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"K\"]},{\"symbol\":\"Q\",\"type\":\"closed coordinate box [-R₀,R₀]^n\",\"scope\":\"R002\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Set Q=∏_{i=1}^n[-R₀,R₀].\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"R₀\",\"n\"]}]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/1/argument\",\"value\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"Fix arbitrary t>0, set J=[t/2,3t/2], and choose compact C from H003 so u(x,s)=q for every x∉C and s∈J. To prove Lebesgue measure finite on every compact, fix arbitrary compact K⊂ℝⁿ. By M016, K is bounded. In the Euclidean norm, boundedness implies there is R₀>0 such that every x∈K satisfies ‖x‖≤R₀; record this as F001: ∃R₀>0, ∀x∈K, ‖x‖≤R₀. The local witness will be chosen from this proved existence in the next paragraph.\",\"uses\":[\"H003\",\"M016\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"t\",\"J\",\"C\",\"K\",\"n\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"There exists R₀>0 such that every x∈K satisfies ‖x‖≤R₀.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"K\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Choose R₀ using F001 and define Q=∏_{i=1}^n[-R₀,R₀]. Each coordinate has absolute value at most ‖x‖, hence K⊆Q. M013 and M014 give μ(Q)=∏_{i=1}^n μ([-R₀,R₀])=(2R₀)^n<∞. Since K is compact in the Hausdorff Euclidean space, it is closed and therefore Borel measurable; monotonicity yields μ(K)≤μ(Q)<∞. As K was arbitrary, Lebesgue measure is finite on compact sets. The Borel measurable structure on ℝⁿ is the σ-algebra generated by the Euclidean open sets, so opens are measurable. Joint smoothness and u=q on the open spatial complement of C throughout J imply all first spatial and time derivatives, and the second and mixed derivatives entering e_t, vanish outside C. Thus e(·,t) is continuous with compact support in C. Apply M001 to conclude e(·,t) is integrable. The same smoothness/support argument shows u_t(·,s), u_{x_j}(·,s), e(·,s), and e_t(·,s) are continuous and vanish off C for each s∈J and j=1,…,n. This proves N001 for arbitrary t>0.\",\"uses\":[\"M013\",\"M014\",\"M001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"R₀\",\"Q\",\"K\",\"C\",\"J\",\"e\",\"u\",\"n\",\"m\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}]}]} }","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration","module"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible; choose a narrow pointer for large objects.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"c4a02e50-f1d6-44b2-9b88-569b19060c51","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":139203,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":122240,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1473,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":403},"total_tokens":140676,"attribution":{"items":{